---
/**
 * Terms of service, written plainly: who runs Inlay, acceptable use, rights in
 * what you open and get back (media editing and AI tools), a takedown route,
 * tips, no guarantee of service, and contact. Inlay is free; the paid HD mode is
 * shelved (docs/hd-mode.md), and "Paid features" keeps room for it returning.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { CONTACT, SELLER, SELLER_KIND, SUPPORT, UPDATED } from '../data/legal'
---

<Page title="Terms · Inlay" description="The terms for using Inlay, its free app and its open-source tracer.">
  <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
    <h1 id="terms-title">Terms</h1>
    <p class="lede">The rules for using Inlay, in plain words.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Inlay (inlaytrace.com) is operated by {SELLER}, {SELLER_KIND} ("we", "us"). You can reach us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. By using the site or the app, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree,
      please don't use them.
    </p>

    <h2>What Inlay is</h2>
    <p>
      Inlay turns images into vector graphics. The app is free: it runs in your browser and your images stay on your device. The
      tracer's source code is open source under the MIT licence; that licence, not these terms, covers the code itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Tips</h2>
    <p>
      You can support Inlay with a tip through <a href={SUPPORT}>Ko-fi</a>. Tips are voluntary gifts: they don't buy a feature, a service or
      priority, and Ko-fi's own terms cover the payment. Ask Ko-fi or email us if a tip was a mistake.
    </p>

    <h2>Paid features</h2>
    <p>
      Inlay has no paid features today. We may add optional ones in the future, such as processing an image on our servers. If we do, their
      price, how payment and refunds work, and any account they need will be set out here before they launch, and the free app will stay
      free.
    </p>
    <p>
      HD mode, a paid beta, has been withdrawn. If you bought HD credits during the beta, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>
      and we'll refund the ones you haven't used.
    </p>

    <h2>Your images and results</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights in the images you open and the results you make. The app processes them on your device; we never receive them,
      and we never use them for anything, including training.
    </p>
    <p>
      You're responsible for having the right to use the images you process and for how you use the results. Results are produced
      automatically and may be inaccurate or incomplete, so check them before you rely on them, especially for anything regulated, like
      medical, legal or engineering work.
    </p>

    <h2>What you may not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law, or process images you don't have the right to use, including anything that infringes someone's copyright or trademark.</li>
      <li>Process sexual images of real people without their consent, any sexual content involving minors, or images meant to harass, threaten, deceive or expose someone (including their private information).</li>
      <li>Use Inlay for fraud, spam or malware.</li>
      <li>Attack, probe, overload or scrape the service, or try to get around its limits or safeguards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting infringing material</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe Inlay is being used to infringe your rights, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> with what you believe is
      infringed and where. We'll look into it promptly and act where it's justified.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep Inlay running and correct, but we can't promise it will always be available or free of errors, and we may change or stop
      features.
    </p>
    <p>
      Inlay, the Inlay name and its logo belong to us. As far as the law allows, Inlay is provided as is, and our total liability to you is
      limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer that can't
      be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms; the date below shows when. Significant changes will be shown on the site before they take effect.</p>

    <p class="fine">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
  </article>
</Page>
